{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools","id":961579,"title":"Carry Laws, Mages, and not getting arrested for carrying your tools","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-01T05:05:10-07:00","id":961579,"title":"Carry Laws, Mages, and not getting arrested for carrying your tools","content":"So my upcoming character is an Obromos mage and very driven to combat (He's Adamant Arrow). His cherished little sister was murdered and taken from him. I was thinking of giving him a sword as one of his magical tools, but if you go walking down Marquette Avenue with a sword on you regardless of open carry laws your going to have problems with the police. I had a thought that I brought up to the ST and she liked it. The sword can be an enhanced item that has a spell worked into it causes it to be, not invisible, but has an aura of &quot;ignore me&quot;, their minds finding the existence of it being there so bland and common place that their mind doesn't pay attention to it at all.<br /> <br /> She liked that idea and she thought that the sword should perhaps also have some utility as a sword too, so the first attack made with it counts as a surprise attack (unexpected) because the enemy's mind ignored the sword, not seeing it as dangerous at all, after it's been used once that scene though any enemy who saw it used is not going to be effected by it's aura at all, and realize it's a very real, dangerous sword. She wanted me to ask some experts if this fits within the nature of magic in Chronicles of Darkness, and that is isn't massively unbalanced, so is this not something that is going to wreck game balance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 09-01-2016, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T05:10:01-07:00","id":961583,"title":"","content":"as a Obrimos, they probably can veil the sword on their own. Forces 2 can make it really invisible, and you could argue that Prime 2 could veil it's symbolic nature of a sword as a weapon, making people look at it and not make a logical jump of &quot;a sword --&gt; it's a dangerous weapon!&quot;, halting at &quot;oh, a sword&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T05:19:28-07:00","id":961586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961583#post961583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as a Obrimos, they probably can veil the sword on their own. Forces 2 can make it really invisible, and you could argue that Prime 2 could veil it's symbolic nature of a sword as a weapon, making people look at it and not make a logical jump of &quot;a sword --&gt; it's a dangerous weapon!&quot;, halting at &quot;oh, a sword&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured a permanently invisible sword has problems all its own in the veins of 'Now where the hell did I leave my sword?' and if something disarms me I can't see it to telekinesis it back to me. Though that Prime idea is pretty much the same thing as the above.<br /> <br /> I got my idea from the Dresden Files and one of the potions Harry used, it made him &quot;invisible&quot; by instead masking him in an aura of &quot;totally uninteresting&quot; so people didn't pay attention to him and just treated him like the janitor or someone who was a part of the daily background noise and not that annoying private investigator always sticking his nose in things.<br /> <br /> Though you are right what I described was more a mind 1-2 concealment; you don't notice it unless you have a reason to be on the lookout for it. Kind of like how retail store employees blend into the background noise of your shopping until you\u2019re looking for them.<br /> <br /> So yeah that prime 2 would work as well, because if I cut someone with it then suddenly I create that connection in them again for the scene. But getting off an unexpected attack isn't too much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":".  Adjusting Grammer and spelling. 09-01-2016, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T05:28:23-07:00","id":961596,"title":"","content":"It's only guaranteed unexpected to Sleepers, but no it isn't too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T05:33:28-07:00","id":961601,"title":"","content":"The question of Carry arms is quite a different one form me but one that I think it's for most people. Living, and also playing Mage in Sweden comes up with some fun and interesting ways about weapons. Many mages, mostly adamant mages though use weapons in their shadow persona as well as tools. If they are outside their sanctum, usually they hid it or carry it concealed or use magic one way or another to conceal them or their weapons just to not interfere with sleeper society. Gun and weapons laws i Sweden are quite a bit more restrict then across the atlantic for the most part if not all parts. You as a civilian can't get a carry permit, neither concealed or open carry. You may transport the gun to and from a shooting range or to the woods for hunting (in right seasons) but getting a concealed carry permit and be able to use it you most more or less be working for the State Police ( think federal) and for use in duty only. etc etc. Even knives, swords, axes, batons, maces, pepperspreys, iron pipes or anything else that can be used as a melee weapon ,can, be illegal to carry in public (depending on the circumstance). But carrying a sword outside a public reenactment tournament is gonna get police attention.<br /> <br /> So how do mages interact with the stricter laws. Weeeeelll they usually don't, cus mage society thinks they are beyond or above sleeper laws, but they still need to accept them in a way. So they continue to hide weapons or mask them with different spells or many just don't bring them unless they expect open confrontation or bring a smaller more consealeble weapon.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the rule question; I wouldn't allow for an auto sneak attack /surprise attack, even if people dont react to it they will react to someone trying to strike at them but i would give it a bonus to the roll for a surprise attack. +1 or maybe even + Potency dice on the roll","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T05:35:21-07:00","id":961602,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Mind 2's Incognito Presence applied to a weapon, which works well. You're basically casting a spell that counts as an automatic success on a Stealth attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T05:35:34-07:00","id":961603,"title":"","content":"As a Forces mage, something being invisible is a laughable problem for you. You probably can localize stuff by changes in the gravity field and stuff like that. Dedicating one slot to reached Nightvision or other &quot;let's have a backup for being blind or against invisible things&quot; is always a wise move.<br /> Though, as an Obrimos, you can ignore spell slots for things like this. Just relinquish it unsafely, and when spell starts causing troubles, dispel it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T05:45:20-07:00","id":961607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961603#post961603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, as an Obrimos, you can ignore spell slots for things like this. Just relinquish it unsafely, and when spell starts causing troubles, dispel it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be warned: Your ST is entirely within their rights to turn the spell into a Havoc at the worst possible time. Like having the spell's Duration fail right as you're talking with a police officer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T06:13:57-07:00","id":961615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961603#post961603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Forces mage, something being invisible is a laughable problem for you. You probably can localize stuff by changes in the gravity field and stuff like that. Dedicating one slot to reached Nightvision or other &quot;let's have a backup for being blind or against invisible things&quot; is always a wise move.<br /> Though, as an Obrimos, you can ignore spell slots for things like this. Just relinquish it unsafely, and when spell starts causing troubles, dispel it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just going to use the Enhanced Item merit for 2 or 3 dots. So I don't know if I can dispell it. I thought once it was added the persistant spell would last until the item is destroyed?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961607#post961607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Be warned: Your ST is entirely within their rights to turn the spell into a Havoc at the worst possible time. Like having the spell's Duration fail right as you're talking with a police officer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was planning to use the Enhanced item merit to give the sword that power. Is that um...possible with a persistant spell that is woven into the item? though I should ask, do Werewolves, Vampires, and Demons count as sleepers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T06:14:34-07:00","id":961616,"title":"","content":"Not really. You roll for it once per day, with one paradox dice per each reach exceeding safe one. So unless you are going really gonzo, it's going to be 1 paradox dice, if not a chance die. Add the fact that if GM uses 1 success to end the spell they are a jerk, because while technically you can spend that one reach to undo advanced duration which will result in spell ending right here right now, &quot;end the spell&quot; is Exceptional Success result for this roll. <br /> So at worst, you are going to dispel this and recast it once per day (less a minute of spellcasting), and at best, you will occasionally get a Condition from the haywire roll which means beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T06:16:41-07:00","id":961617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961615#post961615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just going to use the Enhanced Item merit for 2 or 3 dots. So I don't know if I can dispell it. I thought once it was added the persistant spell would last until the item is destroyed?<br /> <br /> I was planning to use the Enhanced item merit to give the sword that power. Is that um...possible with a persistant spell that is woven into the item? though I should ask, do Werewolves, Vampires, and Demons count as sleepers?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could pay merits dots for it, but you probably could save your merits and use Veiling spells of your Arcana to achieve it without spending merit dots. Depends if you really want to have a sword that's inherently magical, or to make it magical yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T06:26:25-07:00","id":961619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961617#post961617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could pay merits dots for it, but you probably could save your merits and use Veiling spells of your Arcana to achieve it without spending merit dots. Depends if you really want to have a sword that's inherently magical, or to make it magical yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it I feel like I started by veiling it every time I took it out, but then took the time to make it permanently magical on it's own to avoid the complications and headache (probably from containing the paradox) of doing that every day. So, easier on me to just make it into an enhanced object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T06:30:33-07:00","id":961621,"title":"","content":"The tone of the game is definitely more of &quot;should?&quot; rather than &quot;can?&quot;<br /> <br /> That being said, first edition had a mind spell that made things look like other things. For instance, a sword could be made to look like a cane, a pocket watch could look like an iPod, a wand like a pencil, etc. While your character is an Obrimos and not a Mastigos, that doesn't prevent him from trading favors to get such an enchantment on his sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T06:33:43-07:00","id":961622,"title":"","content":"Well, it's 6 seconds of your time every day - 3 to cast it, 3 to dispel it. If you consider that enough pain to pay 2 or 3 experience for it, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T06:42:10-07:00","id":961627,"title":"","content":"Actually, if you are willing to sink 2-3 points into it, you could just make it an Artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:02:34-07:00","id":961635,"title":"","content":"Aren't artifacts remnants of the old world? Why would someone in the old world make a sword that's concealed? Plus I like the idea of having made it myself rather than recovering it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:05:00-07:00","id":961637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961622#post961622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's 6 seconds of your time every day - 3 to cast it, 3 to dispel it. If you consider that enough pain to pay 2 or 3 experience for it, go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly unless it was a grab and go situation I'd probably do it at ritual casting speed and save the paradox for pushing up potency to make it harder to resist that way if I'm fighting a vampire they don't see it coming as it were. I was thinking of it being my dedicated magical tool, so having something extra spiffy like a sword I enhanced myself seems rather fitting for my dedicated tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 09-01-2016, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:11:54-07:00","id":961642,"title":"","content":"as someone who has to carry a sword on the street once per week for medieval sword fencing, i would say a golf club bag work wonders.<br /> <br /> Or if your mage is a fancy one.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://image.rakuten.co.jp/tyokuhan/cabinet/item/bag/img58550788.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> As for the spell, well i, personally, wouldnt let you have a free surprise attack on mages. The sword would ping their mage vision and get a roll (that they might fail).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:15:13-07:00","id":961645,"title":"","content":"Artifacts are items that are somehow infused by Supernal World to the point where they become uniquely magical. Contemporary Mages can't reliably create them, as each artifact is an unique singular phenomena that works under it's own rules. It seems that sometimes an item that you had on you or interacted or grabbed during your Awakening might turn out to be Artifact. A large and powerful storm might turn a car into an artifact. Death of thousands might result in an artifact, and so on.<br /> Each time Supernal World comes closer to the Phenomenal World, it's an occassion for ARtifact to be born.<br /> <br /> If you want to create it, remember that you need Prime 4 to imbue items with spells. If you want to enchant it with a spell you are capable of casting on your own, buying it as a Merit is overpaying. You can cast the spell and relinquish it safely, paing a Willpower dot. Buying the dot back is always 1 XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:18:30-07:00","id":961647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961642#post961642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as someone who has to carry a sword on the street once per week for medieval sword fencing, i would say a golf club bag work wonders.<br /> <br /> Or if your mage is a fancy one.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://image.rakuten.co.jp/tyokuhan/cabinet/item/bag/img58550788.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> As for the spell, well i, personally, wouldnt let you have a free surprise attack on mages. The sword would ping their mage vision and get a roll (that they might fail).</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't. It would ping it the moment when you cast the spell, but not when it's concealed. &quot;Being veilied&quot; is not an active act of magical activity. <br /> Still, a golf bag is a good idea. Just make sure to grab Fast Draw merit to be able to, well, draw it without wasting an action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:20:55-07:00","id":961649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961642#post961642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as someone who has to carry a sword on the street once per week for medieval sword fencing, i would say a golf club bag work wonders.<br /> <br /> Or if your mage is a fancy one.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://image.rakuten.co.jp/tyokuhan/cabinet/item/bag/img58550788.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> As for the spell, well i, personally, wouldnt let you have a free surprise attack on mages. The sword would ping their mage vision and get a roll (that they might fail).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be a lone mage in a Werewolf game...Probably should have mentioned it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961645#post961645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts are items that are somehow infused by Supernal World to the point where they become uniquely magical. Contemporary Mages can't reliably create them, as each artifact is an unique singular phenomena that works under it's own rules. It seems that sometimes an item that you had on you or interacted or grabbed during your Awakening might turn out to be Artifact. A large and powerful storm might turn a car into an artifact. Death of thousands might result in an artifact, and so on.<br /> Each time Supernal World comes closer to the Phenomenal World, it's an occassion for ARtifact to be born.<br /> <br /> If you want to create it, remember that you need Prime 4 to imbue items with spells. If you want to enchant it with a spell you are capable of casting on your own, buying it as a Merit is overpaying. You can cast the spell and relinquish it safely, paing a Willpower dot. Buying the dot back is always 1 XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have another look at artifacts. Sorry, when I think Artifacts I think Exalted, think of something of such amazing power that it would blow mortal minds to look at it in action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:42:38-07:00","id":961661,"title":"","content":"If all you want is a sword you can carry around without worry, you have a few options: Mind (for Incognito Presence), Space (to summon and dismiss it), Forces (invisible), Prime (&quot;I'm not a weapon&quot;), Matter (Shrink or Expand the sword like in the old Legend of Zelda cartoon), <i>possibly</i> Death or Spirit to shift it between Twilight and back.<br /> <br /> Of the options:<br /> Matter might get you flagged for it still being a knife or letter opener (though Matter would help with making the sword out of Perfected materials).<br /> Prime is Ruling, but also kinda reaching in concept, and would likely only affect Sleepers.<br /> Forces is Ruling, but there is still a sword in the way, in addition to the issues you pointed out.<br /> Mind seems like the most exact fit for the effect you want.<br /> Space, I'm not sure the exact level required for moving an object back and forth between a set location and a moving one (your hand).<br /> Spirit, I think the level is higher than desired for shifting back and forth between Twilight. Though some Spirit might be nice if you can convince a Spirit to Fetter itself to your sword for extra bonuses (or if you have a Familiar do the same).<br /> Death is Inferior, and I think you only get to use the Twilight version.<br /> <br /> Making it an Artifact is probably more XP efficient, but kinda Munchkin-y for what you are asking. If you want to use the Artifact's Arcana to patch up a hole in your character, that would make sense, though.<br /> <br /> Since you are in a Werewolf games, silvering the sword (or making sure it is Lunargent - Perfected Silver) is probably a good idea. Matter has a spell (spoiled from Signs of Sorcery) to make materials Perfected, and basic Matter could transmute it to silver as needed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Odd idea, since it is Werewolf, and thus, Spirit/Shadow heavy, I'm wondering if you might be able to contract a Sword-Spirit to serve? Possibly as a Familiar. Give it the shape of an actual sword, and make sure it has the Materialize Manifestation. Need a sword? Have the Spirit Materialize in your hand. Give it the Blast Numen, and &quot;you&quot; can even fling bolts of energy with your sword (Paradox/Dissonance free to boot). Need to be &quot;unarmed&quot;? Have it revert back to Twilight and just follow you around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-01-2016, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:45:31-07:00","id":961662,"title":"","content":"Spirit could also help if you can find a Spirit of Trickery; convince it that making people think this is not a weapon is a great trick to pull off. <br /> While Sword-As-Artifact would need some extra fleshing out, I think it might be interesting. After all, SWORD FROM HEAVENS and other symbolism like this fits a Christian Obrimos very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T08:43:05-07:00","id":961678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961615#post961615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was planning to use the Enhanced item merit to give the sword that power. Is that um...possible with a persistant spell that is woven into the item? though I should ask, do Werewolves, Vampires, and Demons count as sleepers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is and no they do not, respectively. I'd say you could just have someone cast the spell on the item, with an application of Reach to Key it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T08:51:49-07:00","id":961685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961645#post961645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts are items that are somehow infused by Supernal World to the point where they become uniquely magical. Contemporary Mages can't reliably create them, as each artifact is an unique singular phenomena that works under it's own rules. It seems that sometimes an item that you had on you or interacted or grabbed during your Awakening might turn out to be Artifact. A large and powerful storm might turn a car into an artifact. Death of thousands might result in an artifact, and so on.<br /> Each time Supernal World comes closer to the Phenomenal World, it's an occassion for ARtifact to be born.<br /> <br /> If you want to create it, remember that you need Prime 4 to imbue items with spells. If you want to enchant it with a spell you are capable of casting on your own, buying it as a Merit is overpaying. You can cast the spell and relinquish it safely, paing a Willpower dot. Buying the dot back is always 1 XP.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Another &quot;common&quot; means to acquire artifacts (or justify their existence) is that they are provided by supernal beings in connection with their summoning and tests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:15:34-07:00","id":961749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961685#post961685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Another &quot;common&quot; means to acquire artifacts (or justify their existence) is that they are provided by supernal beings in connection with their summoning and tests.</div> </div> </div> </div>So an idea might be to summon a Seraph or Cherubim and request the sword of them?<br /> <br /> So I guess the next thing to ask is the same thing I'd ask for an exalted artifact? What do I want this sword to do?<br /> <br /> -Conceal.<br /> - combat functionality so I'm not left eating Werewolf dust.<br /> <br /> humm...Invisability cast on self, quickened...would be forces 2...<br /> <br /> What would be a good combat utility ability?<br /> My first thought is to pull in Aetheric flames to coat the sword in the power to smite my foes as an angel would. But a cherub's flaming sword seems a bit cliche. Any advice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:21:13-07:00","id":961754,"title":"","content":"Dispellation. Since you've read the DF think Morgan's sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:25:45-07:00","id":961763,"title":"","content":"If you go for dispellation, make sure you go for 4th dot version, not 1st dot version. Still, I don't think that a guest mage pc in a werewolf party will get a lot of mileage from supernal dispellation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:30:44-07:00","id":961768,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd get more mileage out of something like fire. My likely enemies are Vampires, and/or demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T11:18:21-07:00","id":961793,"title":"","content":"Have the gift be a cane-sword instead of I dunno, a broadsword/katana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T11:33:30-07:00","id":961797,"title":"","content":"Artifacts have Arcana that the user can utilize, so something the Mage doesn't already possess might be useful. Despite Death being an inferior Arcana for the Aether (and thus, Obrimos), maybe use that? Supernal Entities can have one other Arcana than their &quot;Ruling&quot; one, and I don't think they have restrictions regarding Inferior Arcana. And having an Angel give you a sword (or sword-cane) of Death is just begging for elaboration and story. The Death Arcana will help against Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T11:56:44-07:00","id":961805,"title":"","content":"Axel has it right, Incognito Presence is what you're looking for, man.<br /> <br /> And just because you're in a Werewolf game doesn't mean that you're not going to be up against other Mages -- quite the opposite, in fact. First off, Mages and Werewolves often come into conflict over resources -- many Hallows form on Ley Line nexii, which also conveniently spawn Loci frequently.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the Shadow's denizens are actively hostile toward all but a small subset of Mages (those with Spirit 4+), and that includes Werewolves. So yeah, have fun with that. The pack tou run with might make exceptions because they know you, but every other werewolf you encounter is going to see you as an interloper, Forsaken and Pure alike.<br /> <br /> My advice: learn the Prime Veiling effect that changes your Nimbus type as a Rote, pronto. You're going to be using it a shit-ton.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","user":"Raikirah","date":". 09-01-2016, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:07:09-07:00","id":961814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raikirah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961805#post961805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but every other werewolf you encounter is going to see you as an interloper, Forsaken and Pure alike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure 2E has dropped that aspect. Werewolves only care about you in direct regard as it impacts them or their territory.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:10:36-07:00","id":961817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961797#post961797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts have Arcana that the user can utilize, so something the Mage doesn't already possess might be useful. Despite Death being an inferior Arcana for the Aether (and thus, Obrimos), maybe use that? Supernal Entities can have one other Arcana than their &amp;quot;Ruling&amp;quot; one, and I don't think they have restrictions regarding Inferior Arcana. And having an Angel give you a sword (or sword-cane) of Death is just begging for elaboration and story. The Death Arcana will help against Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>The direct quote is &quot;effective arcana&quot; this means they can pretend to have arcana for the effects they allow you to cast so you can determine Reach. It's not the same thing as having all of Death or whatever at your disposal simply because you have an artifact with a Death effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:13:42-07:00","id":961820,"title":"","content":"To avoid the carry a deadly weapon in public issue, simply have the Cherubim or Seraphim gift the mage a normally harmless or otherwise inconspicuous object such as a ring or bracelet that transforms into a sword or other weapon (or &quot;summons&quot; it from mana using Prime). There's no reason not to be creative with artifacts.<br /> <br /> Note also that some of the other great benefits that Prime can offer a weapon is the ability to injure ephemeral objects and beings and deal aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:33:05-07:00","id":961838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961814#post961814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure 2E has dropped that aspect. Werewolves only care about you in direct regard as it impacts them or their territory.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inferring that from the section on the Spirit 4 Attainment, which says that once you've gotten it that &quot;spirits no longer react to your presence with open hostility&quot;.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are (partially) denizens of the Shadow, much more so than Mages, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T12:46:41-07:00","id":961846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raikirah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961838#post961838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm inferring that from the section on the Spirit 4 Attainment, which says that once you've gotten it that &quot;spirits no longer react to your presence with open hostility&quot;.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are (partially) denizens of the Shadow, much more so than Mages, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are and they aren't. They are kinda part spirit, but their mentality is closer to human. As for Spirits not liking Mages, that probably has to do with Spirits being at risk from a Mage reprogramming them, butting in where they aren't welcome, and being far more resistant to being bullied around compared to most humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:35:54-07:00","id":961872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961846#post961846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolves are and they aren't. They are kinda part spirit, but their mentality is closer to human. As for Spirits not liking Mages, that probably has to do with Spirits being at risk from a Mage reprogramming them, butting in where they aren't welcome, and being far more resistant to being bullied around compared to most humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I'm getting at -- they're unwelcome. A Mage in the Shadow is the equivalent of a high-class Manhattan lawyer driving his Porsche up to a biker bar with a group of Hell's Angel's in residence. The reception he gets is going to be far from friendly, with the bar's inhabitants looking for the smallest excuse to take umbridge and throw down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:52:23-07:00","id":961886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raikirah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961872#post961872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's exactly what I'm getting at -- they're unwelcome. A Mage in the Shadow is the equivalent of a high-class Manhattan lawyer driving his Porsche up to a biker bar with a group of Hell's Angel's in residence. The reception he gets is going to be far from friendly, with the bar's inhabitants looking for the smallest excuse to take umbridge and throw down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give that lawyer a weapon or a special forces team, and you are closer. Spirits probably resent Mages because they are <i>playthings</i> to a Mage with a good enough grasp of Spirit. Like, they can literally be reprogramed to the Mage's desire for convenience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T04:32:51-07:00","id":962196,"title":"","content":"I had the exact problem with my Moros Mage and his katana. Incognito Presence (Mind) would solve your problem, as would Hidden Hoard (Matter). If you have to get it through some kind of security you could also include Machine Invisibility (Matter) and walk right through those detectors at the airport, just make sure you are not selected for a pat down. I would suggest simply casting the spell again each day and use an advanced duration to prevent causing those pesky Havocs.<br /> I myself utilise runes in the casting. I altered the hilt and sheath of the katana to combine into a rune, which I use to focus the spell. If I ever need to draw my sword I automatically break the spell and free up a spell slot. If you incorporate a quickdraw technique into your combat style it would still give you that surprise element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:33:17-07:00","id":962501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zaephyrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=962196#post962196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had the exact problem with my Moros Mage and his katana. Incognito Presence (Mind) would solve your problem, as would Hidden Hoard (Matter). If you have to get it through some kind of security you could also include Machine Invisibility (Matter) and walk right through those detectors at the airport, just make sure you are not selected for a pat down. I would suggest simply casting the spell again each day and use an advanced duration to prevent causing those pesky Havocs.<br /> I myself utilise runes in the casting. I altered the hilt and sheath of the katana to combine into a rune, which I use to focus the spell. If I ever need to draw my sword I automatically break the spell and free up a spell slot. If you incorporate a quickdraw technique into your combat style it would still give you that surprise element.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I will do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:47:15-07:00","id":962509,"title":"","content":"So here is what I figured out for my artifact.<br /> <br /> The blade was gifted to me by the Seraphim Sudrushael. The sword is the physical manifestation of righteous wrath, and judgement forged in the heart of Aether from the concepts of victory, steel, and battle. It was tempered in the idea of nobility, and honed against the wheel of duty. It's guard has the appearance of gold and shaped into two angelic forms with their wings out stretched their hands caressing the blade, and the blade shines with a luster of mirror polished metal. <br /> <br /> It was gifted to me for service to the angel, durring the day that my body slumbered while my soul was in Aether, for how long I cannot guess, my journy to the watchtower was interupted when following my guide Lashaelmuel I spotted a woman in danger. She shouted at me to not leave the path or my soul would be in peril, but She was in danger something was going to kill her and I couldn't stand by and do nothing. Of course I hadn't signed my name to the tower yet so, as far as magic went I had none and I was about to step in to a battle between a Seraph and a\u2026you know I never found out what that was? Some sort of beast of the realm I'm guessing. Maybe an invasive spirit from another supernal realm? Either way she was loseing to it and would soon be torn apart, so I did the only thing I knew to do. The stupid man thing. I picked up a rock and flung it. Yep, humanity has come so far, look at us flinging rocks instead of stool.<br /> <br /> Either way that rock hit it clean in the head and got it's attention Lashaelmuel looked on in horror, muttering something about not loseing this one, and other things that sounded like she would be in big trouble if I died. Funny how the senses liven up with you channelge a Lion the size of a grizzlebear to a fight and your armed with\u2026rocks.<br /> <br /> I probably should have died there but when your sleep walking the path of aether you do have a small edge. You can see your death coming, and that is the differnce between being reduced to a red schemer and living to see another day. So I did the only logical thing looking at this thing coming to reduce me to a lumpy red sauce. I reached down and grabbed another rock as I rolled under its cleaver Claws.<br /> <br /> Many rocks later the woman came limping over and I realized she was an angel. To reward me and and apparently dodge a life debt she offered me her sword, her littoral sword. I politely refused twice before accepting the third time figuring it would be rude not to at that point.<br /> <br /> When I awoke after the ordeal the sword was there next to me.<br /> <br /> The blade burns with angelic wrath, calling upon it the fires of Aether. This power is automatically cast when the blade is drawn, and lasts until it is returned to it's scabbard or the second power is used. As a by product of this effect the temperature in any room or location drops by 20 degrees, as the blade draws in and magnifies the ambient thermal energy. For 1 mana per attack this damage may strike empheral targets.<br /> <br /> The blade also has one other power. It may call forth a pillar of angelic golden flame, this counts as a blast with a damage of 2, A blast area of 3, and a force of 3. The damage counts as coming from fire for the purposes of weaknesses and immunities, and for a mana the blast area damage may hit empheral targets.<br /> <br /> This effect cancels the first, which may be reactivated by succeeding on a 4 die roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 09-02-2016, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T15:41:36-07:00","id":962537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=961886#post961886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Give that lawyer a weapon or a special forces team, and you are closer. Spirits probably resent Mages because they are <i>playthings</i> to a Mage with a good enough grasp of Spirit. Like, they can literally be reprogramed to the Mage's desire for convenience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages high enough Ranked (influence intended) to do so are at Adept level or above, and thus have the Spirit 4 Attainment. So no, the spirits don't resent those Mages automatically. After all, other higher-Ranked Spirits mess with low-ranked spirits' mojo all of the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regardless, this entire debate is a non-sequitur -- the point is that a Mage dealing with Werewolves is in a hostile environment. OP is an Obrimos iirc, and unless he wants to focus Spirit for some reason, he's going to be needing to camouflage himself as Kin so as not to become chunky salsa. As my old Werewolf GM used to put it, &quot;roll for meat.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T15:54:28-07:00","id":962543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raikirah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=962537#post962537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regardless, this entire debate is a non-sequitur -- the point is that a Mage dealing with Werewolves is in a hostile environment. OP is an Obrimos iirc, and unless he wants to focus Spirit for some reason, he's going to be needing to camouflage himself as Kin so as not to become chunky salsa. As my old Werewolf GM used to put it, &quot;roll for meat.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In the CofD, mages and werewolves have no inherent hostility to one another. The interaction between a mage and a werewolf or pack will depend entirely on the nature and conduct of the particular mage and werewolves.<br /> <br /> If you want to see examples of how mages and werewolves could interact, including mages as part of a werewolf pack, you should read the relevant sections of The Pack for Werewolf 2e. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T16:06:58-07:00","id":962547,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> You don't need to have static stats like that for the effects the sword produces, its abilities are similar to Rotes that you can spend Reach on and apply dice penalties to its pool of whatever its effective arcana+gnosis is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T16:17:37-07:00","id":962551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=962547#post962547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar600_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"600\" data-vbnamecard=\"600\">HaplessWithDice</a> You don't need to have static stats like that for the effects the sword produces, its abilities are similar to Rotes that you can spend Reach on and apply dice penalties to its pool of whatever its effective arcana+gnosis is.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I have to roll for them?<br /> <br /> Ummm....let's see what would you rate the first one at? It's a arcana 2 I think, with a -2 to pool for increased potency and 1 reach for instant cast, 1 for advanced duration 1 scene.<br /> <br /> The second is arcana 4? 1 reach for instant cast, -2 for increased potency. Umm. That seems right? And I was thinking the attack roll for that should be (6 sword arcana + gnosis) + weaponry - defense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 09-02-2016, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T17:58:11-07:00","id":962600,"title":"","content":"Just thought of this but don't metal detectors use magnetic fields? Can't forces mages warp magnetic fields?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T17:59:48-07:00","id":962603,"title":"","content":"You'll probably want to spend Reach on Instant Cast too. Artifacts can possibly Paradox so you know. I don't know exactly what your dice pool looks like, but you're going to want to talk to your ST about what she's comfortable letting it have for &quot;effective&quot; arcana and gnosis. You can probably go with the minimums, so Prime 4 and Gnosis...3?<br /> <br /> Yes, Forces can manipulate magnetic fields.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T18:00:21-07:00","id":962604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=962600#post962600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just thought of this but don't metal detectors use magnetic fields? Can't forces mages warp magnetic fields?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magnetism is definitely under the purview of Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T18:08:00-07:00","id":962611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=962603#post962603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll probably want to spend Reach on Instant Cast too. Artifacts can possibly Paradox so you know. I don't know exactly what your dice pool looks like, but you're going to want to talk to your ST about what she's comfortable letting it have for &amp;quot;effective&amp;quot; arcana and gnosis. You can probably go with the minimums, so Prime 4 and Gnosis...3?<br /> <br /> Yes, Forces can manipulate magnetic fields.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm at work so I can't check the book but I thought gnosis for the artifact was 1/2 dot cost, and that was equal to the highest arcana used.....Ohhh it's a 5 dot because of the first power adding 1/2 its value. Did I figure those values right? And wait do I need to include that draw back?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T19:32:04-07:00","id":962643,"title":"","content":"No idea. I'll try to remember to double check in the morning, but someone who has recently (re)read the rules will probably beat me to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T19:48:18-07:00","id":963494,"title":"","content":"Okay so this is what I went with an enhanced object. So the sword will be...<br /> Dumanium double bladed sword. (2 mana charges, +2 damage)<br /> Invisibility (forces 2)<br /> Superlative Luck Melee (Fate 3)<br /> <br /> This should be a 5 dot item...I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T06:45:51-07:00","id":963668,"title":"","content":"If it's an artifact it goes as follows -<br /> The base value is the highest arcanum used, or three, whichever is higher. Each power after that adds half of the highest arcanum rounded up. So in this case it would be a 7 dot item, or 6 dot if the GM wants to be generous and just halve the two secondary spells and add them up. (3 (Fate) + 2 (half of fate, rounded up) +2)<br /> <br /> If it's an enhanced item, and so all the spells are constant, it would be -<br /> Dots of spells, in effect, and dots over 5 only count for half as the book says. So in this case it would be a 13 dot item.<br /> 3 (Luck) + 2 (Invisibility) + 4 (+2 damage and +2 mana? not sure) equals 9, that's 4 over 5 which need to be doubled and hence 5 + 4*2 gives us 13.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T07:05:10-07:00","id":963677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961579-carry-laws-mages-and-not-getting-arrested-for-carrying-your-tools?p=963668#post963668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's an artifact it goes as follows -<br /> The base value is the highest arcanum used, or three, whichever is higher. Each power after that adds half of the highest arcanum rounded up. So in this case it would be a 7 dot item, or 6 dot if the GM wants to be generous and just halve the two secondary spells and add them up. (3 (Fate) + 2 (half of fate, rounded up) +2)<br /> <br /> If it's an enhanced item, and so all the spells are constant, it would be -<br /> Dots of spells, in effect, and dots over 5 only count for half as the book says. So in this case it would be a 13 dot item.<br /> 3 (Luck) + 2 (Invisibility) + 4 (+2 damage and +2 mana? not sure) equals 9, that's 4 over 5 which need to be doubled and hence 5 + 4*2 gives us 13.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just looked that up Your right partly I miss calculated its full dots up to 5, then half dots after. Forge Dumanium is a 4 dot matter spell which if counted as one of the spells woven into my item, which I can see the argument for I was just adding a dot for it. So in total that is 9 dots. Halve the 4 dots after that and...we get +2 so 7 dot Enhanced Item. Which leaves me with 3 dots in character creation pull the rest of my character together. Which may be tough. Very tough. So, I'll probably have to skip on that front. Which is a shame. 6 dots was the maximum of my budget.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}